## What the earlier session found (evidence and caveats)
- Old run (arrival rate 1.0, horizon 2000, 3 eval seeds, one checkpoint per arm, 3 agents): tasks completed centralised 168/17/166, section 352/364/370, decentralised 405/417/352. Capacity is about 0.2 tasks per step, so at 1.0 the backlog grew without limit and no agent was ever idle. The centralised arm parked 1 to 2 agents for 92 to 99 percent of steps, and in seed 6 deadlocked from step ~173. Its training returns collapsed repeatedly.
- The reward is shaping + n_deliver*delivery - n_blocked*override - n_cng*congestion. Congestion is live (small). Shaping telescopes, so an episode return can only go clearly negative through the override term.
- 12-iteration test (horizon 500, arrival 0.15): episode_return_mean rose from 90 to 705 by iteration 8, then collapsed to -323 at iteration 11, with override rate 0.63. The final evaluation trace (seed 5) shows a head-on swap deadlock in the single-lane corridor 20-21-22 of the example instance. Vertex 22 is the only dead end in the graph, a delivery vertex, and the most used delivery goal. 19 of 63 released tasks were completed, the last at step 189, then 311 steps (190 to 500) without a completion. 47.6 percent of all agent-steps were overridden (agents 1/2/3: 38.6/46.4/57.8 percent). Agents 1 (leaving 22) and 3 (entering) tried to swap in 150 of the 311 stalled steps, so the deadlock is symmetric, not a frozen blocker. This is one short run, one seed and an early policy: check whether it recurs before generalising.
- Per-iteration rates depend strongly on the episode phase (the return rate falls by a factor of 2 to 10 after the first ~450 steps in all arms), which is why every runner now finishes exactly one episode per iteration.

## What is now in the code
- reward_terms and per-episode progress keys: return_shaping, return_deliver, return_override, return_congestion, override_rate, episode_tasks_completed, episode_tasks_released, episode_max_agent_override_share, episode_step, plus the older snapshot keys.
- Training seeds start at a per-runner offset.
- One episode-length parameter `--horizon` (default 2000), shared by training and evaluation. build_ppo_config sets rollout_fragment_length = horizon and train_batch_size = max(num_env_runners,1) * horizon, so episode_return_mean exists on every iteration (RLlib's default batch of 4000 cannot be combined with a horizon-sized fragment). With 7 runners the default 2000 samples 14000 steps per iteration, so use ~630 (4410 steps per iteration: about 1130 iterations for 5M steps, 114 for the 500000 steps actually used). num_epochs and minibatch_size are unchanged and may need retuning (minibatch_size must be at most the batch).
- `--arrival-rate` (default 1.0) and one WAIT_COST = 2.0 in example 04; nothing in src/ reads c_wait. `--communication` (default off) on 04 and 04b, decentralised only; the thesis' conditional ablation RQ5, to be run as a separate condition. Traces do not record messages.
- viz/training_run.py: `python -m slap_mapd_coupling.viz.training_run --run-dir DIR --out OUT` writes training_progress.png, trace_<arm>_episode_<n>.png and trace_comparison.png (two or more traces) and prints per-trace numbers (completed, longest stretch without a completion, per-agent moved / waited / overridden shares, most repeated overridden moves, head-on swap steps). It copes with older logs.
- Lint: CI was already red before this work (black on 7 files, flake8 on zones.py:96 and a blank line at the end of test_checkpoint_layout.py). This work added 4 flake8 E501 lines (over 100 characters) in examples/04_decentralised_training.py, near lines 51, 53, 132 and 133. Fix those in a small branch, and ask before reformatting the unrelated files.

## What was actually run (2026-10-14, measured from the folders, logs and ray_results)
The plan in an earlier version of this note (a 5M-step budget and `mv` into one folder per condition) did not happen as written. All runs used `--horizon=630 --arrival-rate=0.15 --env-runners=7 --gpu --eval-seeds=3 --budget-env-steps=500000`, so 114 iterations of 4410 steps per arm (502740 steps sampled, over the budget by 2740). The progress file and traces always go to examples/output/ and are truncated at the start of a run.
- Sanity pass (50000 steps, 12 iterations, decentralised only): ~/thesis_runs/sanity_h630. It also holds older material (instance PNGs, an older checkpoint copy). Earlier output from before the horizon change: ~/thesis_runs/before_h630.
- Three arms in the order 04 (decentralised), 02 (centralised), 03 (section), 11:05 to 12:02: ~/thesis_runs/h630_rate0.15, logs ~/thesis_runs/run_0{4_decentralised_training,2_centralised_fixed,3_section_based}_h630_rate0.15.log. The `mv examples/output ~/thesis_runs/h630_rate0.15` that ended the loop failed (the target existed and was not empty), so the three arms share one output folder. Each arm has traces/<arm>_episode_{1,2,3}.jsonl and <arm>_training_progress.jsonl.
- The decentralised progress file was truncated to 0 bytes when the communication run started in the same examples/output. It was rebuilt from the Ray trial's result.json (~/ray_results/decentralised_fixed_only/PPO_*74804*) with example 04's own iteration_record. The same procedure reproduces the centralised and section progress files byte for byte, and iterations 1 and 114 match the log. So the decentralised file is a reconstruction (same keys, same values), not the file the run wrote.
- Checkpoints (under ~/ray_results/<arm>_fixed_only/, the path is on the "Checkpoint saved" line of each log): decentralised PPO_*74804* (10-44-23), centralised PPO_*7396c* (11-05-50), section PPO_*6170e* (11-33-57). Other trials in ray_results are older runs.
- Communication-on condition (`04 --communication`, decentralised only): ran out of CUDA memory on four attempts (the first at 12:02, with the original code). The first attempt's log is ~/thesis_runs/run_04_h630_rate0.15_comm.log, and its truncated output is the empty decentralised file mentioned above. The other three left only empty progress files, which were deleted. The cause is in the section below. The fifth attempt, with the fix, started at about 12:23 and finished without error (exit code 0): 114 iterations, 502740 steps sampled, 3 evaluation traces. Its log is ~/thesis_runs/run_04_h630_rate0.15_comm_retry.log. Its checkpoint is ~/ray_results/decentralised_fixed_only/PPO_warehouse_mapd_multi_agent_env_11490_00000_0_2026-10-14_12-21-49/checkpoint_000000. The author moves its output to ~/thesis_runs/h630_rate0.15_comm. If that folder does not exist, the output is still in examples/output. A checkpoint trained with --communication must be evaluated with the same flag in 04b_evaluate_checkpoint.py (it checks and raises on a mismatch).
- Measured, printed at the end of each log (share of goal moves that bring a robot closer, pooled over the 3 evaluation episodes, one checkpoint per arm, so no confidence interval): centralised 91%, decentralised 90%, decentralised with communication 89%, section 87%. These are close and rest on 3 episodes per arm, so they say nothing yet about a difference between arms. Tasks completed and deadlocks are not in this note, analyse them from the traces.
- Evaluation shares the horizon (630 steps), so results are not comparable with the old 2000-step ones.
- Commands to repeat a run, in fish, from the main checkout (move examples/output away first, and move it again after each run):
    PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True ~/.venvs/rl/bin/python examples/04_decentralised_training.py --horizon=630 --arrival-rate=0.15 --env-runners=7 --gpu --budget-env-steps=500000 --eval-seeds=3 [--communication] 2>&1 | tee ~/thesis_runs/<name>.log
  Use 02_centralised_fixed.py or 03_section_based.py for the other arms. Do not rely on one `mv` into an existing folder.

## The out-of-memory fix (commit 8de84f0 on branch fix/chunk-value-pass, not pushed)
- Measured: the communication run died in the first iteration, inside RLlib's GAE connector, which calls `compute_values` once on the whole train batch (4410 steps) before any minibatching. With communication on, the encoder's per-edge tensors for all steps at once need 1.25 GiB more than the GPU had (8 GiB card, the process at 4.5 to 5.6 GiB). `minibatch_size` is not involved, and `expandable_segments` did not help.
- Change: ActionMaskingTorchRLModule.compute_values (src/slap_mapd_coupling/environment/action_masking.py) runs batches above VALUE_CHUNK_ROWS = 512 rows in chunks, under torch.no_grad(). The first version without no_grad still ran out of memory, because the chunks kept their autograd graphs. The GAE connector turns the values into numpy, and the loss calls compute_values on a 128-row minibatch or with embeddings, so those stay differentiable. Test: tests/unit/test_rl_module.py::test_the_value_is_the_same_when_computed_in_chunks (communication off and on). The 18 tests of test_rl_module.py and test_action_masking.py pass.
- Inferred, not measured on a full run: values agree with the unchunked ones up to float rounding, so the other arms (which fit in memory and ran unchunked) stay comparable with the communication run. The thesis chapters say nothing about how values are batched.
- The main checkout is on this branch. The staged thesis-progress/scripts/Images PNGs, the .gitignore change and the examples/00b edit were left uncommitted. The author opens the PR: give the PR text in chat.

